+// g-lab-bit fork (annot_undo_wrap.patch)
+// Experimental API.
+// Re-presents |annot|'s normal appearance without changing it: /AP /N becomes
+// a NEW form that draws the ORIGINAL form unchanged ("q /O Do Q"), then, if
+// |tint_rgb| (3 floats in [0,1]) is given, a tint in that colour clipped by the
+// original's alpha (soft mask) and blended /Color, so the original's lightness
+// shows through; the whole content is wrapped in nested /OC marked content for
+// the OCGs |ocg_indices| (outermost first), so PDFium and pdf.js hide it with
+// any of them. The wrapper records the original (/RpOriginal); wrapping a
+// wrapper rewraps the original. No tint and no layers puts the original back.
+// Only the annotation's own dictionary (and its /Annots holder for a direct
+// one) changes; an indirect /AP dictionary is replaced by a direct copy.
+// Returns false (nothing changed) without a normal appearance stream, for an
+// invalid colour or layer index.
